course: dictionary
lesson: 11853
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word bobble is one of them. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «Mia's red hat has a big bobble on top.» Here a bobble is a small soft ball of wool, because hats have bobbles.
explain: «Dad's old jumper is covered in bobbles.» Now the bobbles are tiny balls of fluff. Old jumpers get them after lots of wear, so the clues in the sentence point to fluff, not wool.
explain: Bobble can also be a verb, an action word. «The ball bobbled over the bumpy pitch.» The ball moved up and down unsteadily, like a ball on bumpy ground. Ask yourself: does the sentence show an object or an action? That tells you the meaning.
explain: In American sport, to bobble means to fumble, which is to drop a ball you should have caught. «The American player bobbled the catch and the ball hit the ground.» The word catch and the words hit the ground are your clues.
fact: A bobble is a small soft ball of wool on top of a woolly hat, or on the end of a string.
fact: A bobble hat is a woolly hat that has a bobble on it.
fact: A bobble is also a tiny ball of fluff that forms on an old jumper or blanket after a lot of wear. This is also called a pill.
fact: «To bobble» means to bounce or move up and down unsteadily, like a ball on bumpy ground.
fact: In American sport, «to bobble the ball» means to fumble it, to fail to catch or hold it cleanly.
exercise: «Mia's red hat has a big bobble on top.» What is the bobble? | A loud noise | A kind of shoe | *A small soft ball of wool | A pair of gloves
exercise: «The ball bobbled over the bumpy ground.» What does bobbled mean? | Shone brightly | Stood still and quiet | *Bounced up and down unsteadily | Ran smoothly and fast
exercise: «Dad's old jumper is covered in bobbles.» Find and copy one word that means tiny balls of fluff. | covered | old | jumper | *bobbles
test: In «The American player bobbled the catch», what does bobbled mean? | *Fumbled and dropped it | Caught it perfectly | Kicked it high | Ran away with it
test: Which word in «The ball bobbled on the bumpy pitch» is a verb? | pitch | *bobbled | bumpy | ball
exam: Ruby says a bobble is a kind of shoe. What is a bobble really? | A tall, thin bird | *A small soft ball of wool, like the one on a hat | A loud bang in a football match | A kind of shoe worn in the snow
